      "start_seconds": 1.07,
      "end_seconds": 3.66,
      "duration_seconds": 2.59,
      "text": "hello, come in. Mind the step"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 5.59,
      "end_seconds": 8.52,
      "duration_seconds": 2.93,
      "text": "morning, doctor, sorry about the rush"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 10.31,
      "end_seconds": 13.07,
      "duration_seconds": 2.76,
      "text": "so what can I do for you?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 14.71,
      "end_seconds": 19.19,
      "duration_seconds": 4.48,
      "text": "Doctor it's swelling. It's getting on my nerves now."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 21.04,
      "end_seconds": 25.06,
      "duration_seconds": 4.02,
      "text": "Are you taking anything regularly, including from the pharmacy?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 27.04,
      "end_seconds": 36.71,
      "duration_seconds": 9.67,
      "text": "Furosemide i take it 40 milligrams every morning for the fluid work has been very busy so I kept ignoring it"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 37.45,
      "end_seconds": 38.7,
      "duration_seconds": 1.25,
      "text": "since when exactly?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 39.41,
      "end_seconds": 43.43,
      "duration_seconds": 4.02,
      "text": "So, I've had it for one week."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 44.57,
      "end_seconds": 46.73,
      "duration_seconds": 2.16,
      "text": "how frequently does it come?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 47.72,
      "end_seconds": 50.25,
      "duration_seconds": 2.53,
      "text": "I'd say on and off."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 51.99,
      "end_seconds": 54.8,
      "duration_seconds": 2.81,
      "text": "have you noticed anything else alongside it?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 56.81,
      "end_seconds": 61.85,
      "duration_seconds": 5.04,
      "text": "Difficulty walking goes along with it, most of the time"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 67.8,
      "end_seconds": 73.4,
      "duration_seconds": 5.6,
      "text": "right, any fever, pop or crack or pain in the knee at all?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 74.84,
      "end_seconds": 78.34,
      "duration_seconds": 3.5,
      "text": "No, none of those at all."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 78.74,
      "end_seconds": 83.7,
      "duration_seconds": 4.96,
      "text": "right, right. Alright, any pins and needles or loss of strength anywhere?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 84.78,
      "end_seconds": 86.15,
      "duration_seconds": 1.37,
      "text": "nothing odd there"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 93.78,
      "end_seconds": 96.93,
      "duration_seconds": 3.15,
      "text": "has anyone ever diagnosed you with something?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 98.76,
      "end_seconds": 101.9,
      "duration_seconds": 3.14,
      "text": "I have heart failure for five years"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 109.57,
      "end_seconds": 113.62,
      "duration_seconds": 4.05,
      "text": "Let's talk a little about your daily life and habits."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 115.3,
      "end_seconds": 138.07,
      "duration_seconds": 22.77,
      "text": "No, I've never smoked in my life. I used to drink heavily but I stopped four years ago. No, I share a house with my brother. Not much, I mostly stay in these days. I look after my grandchildren most days"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 139.94,
      "end_seconds": 145.58,
      "duration_seconds": 5.64,
      "text": "are you allergic to anything? Any allergies to to medicines or foods?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 147.17,
      "end_seconds": 150.44,
      "duration_seconds": 3.27,
      "text": "no, nothing as far as I know"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 165.37,
      "end_seconds": 167.83,
      "duration_seconds": 2.46,
      "text": "I'll do your observations first"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 181.21,
      "end_seconds": 183.6,
      "duration_seconds": 2.39,
      "text": "That's it just a little longer..."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 198.17,
      "end_seconds": 207.41,
      "duration_seconds": 9.24,
      "text": "Okay: blood pressure 125 over 80 temp 37.0 degrees pulse is 86 beats a minute SpO2 98 percent on room air."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 209.9,
      "end_seconds": 214.45,
      "duration_seconds": 4.55,
      "text": "let me look at the area, I'll be gentle"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 215.57,
      "end_seconds": 216.95,
      "duration_seconds": 1.38,
      "text": "Does that hurt?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 225.64,
      "end_seconds": 232.55,
      "duration_seconds": 6.91,
      "text": "There's swelling and bruising on the outer side of the ankle, tender over the ligament."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 236.03,
      "end_seconds": 237.72,
      "duration_seconds": 1.69,
      "text": "That's the examination finished."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 250.46,
      "end_seconds": 258.6,
      "duration_seconds": 8.14,
      "text": "so based on the history and the examination I think we're dealing with an ankle sprain at this stage"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 259.72,
      "end_seconds": 261.07,
      "duration_seconds": 1.35,
      "text": "is this permanent?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 261.58,
      "end_seconds": 291.03,
      "duration_seconds": 29.45,
      "text": "Nothing I've seen today points to an emergency. It looks like an ankle sprain but I'd like to confirm. Let's get an X-ray of the ankle for ankle injury. I'm going to put you on ibuprofen 400 milligrams three times a day after food for three days. That's for ankle pain. I'll put all of this in writing so so you don't have to remember it."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 291.6,
      "end_seconds": 320.14,
      "duration_seconds": 28.54,
      "text": "rest, ice for twenty minutes at a a time, a compression bandage and keep the foot up i'd like you to see physiotherapy as well, and I'll write the referral keep an eye out, and if the symptoms get worse, call us the same day or go to emergency is there anything you'd like me to go over again?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 321.87,
      "end_seconds": 327.68,
      "duration_seconds": 5.81,
      "text": "sorry, what was I saying, no, that's all. Thanks a lot"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 329.75,
      "end_seconds": 331.23,
      "duration_seconds": 1.48,
      "text": "See you soon."
    }
  ]
}